==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|veikr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|waikwaz|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈveiːkʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eiːkʏr|lang=is}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj-01|veik|veikt|veikari|veikastur}}

# [[weak]], [[pliant]]
# [[sick]], [[ill]]
#: ''Hún er '''veik'''.''
#:: She's '''sick'''.
#: ''Hann er '''veikur'''.''
#:: He's '''sick'''.
#: ''[[barn#Icelandic|Barnið]] er '''veikt'''.''
#:: The [[child]] is '''sick'''.
# {{context|of a sound|lang=is}} [[faint]], [[low]]
# {{music|lang=is}} [[soft]], [[piano]]
# {{grammar|lang=is}} [[weak]]

====Inflection====
{{is-decl-adj-1|v|ei|k}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|weak}} {{l|is|aumur}}
* {{sense|sick}} {{l|is|sjúkur}}, {{l|is|lasinn}}
* {{sense|faint, low}} {{l|is|daufur}}, {{l|is|lágur}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|weak}} {{l|is|sterkur}}, {{l|is|traustur}}, {{l|is|öflugur}}
* {{sense|sick}} {{l|is|frískur}}, {{l|is|heilbrigður}}, {{l|is|heill}}
* {{sense|faint, low}} {{l|is|hár}}, {{l|is|hávær}}
* {{sense|(''music'') soft}} {{l|is|sterkur}}
* {{sense|(''grammar'') weak}} {{l|is|sterkur}}

